* se-receiver-dm-pex -- sky130 single-ended D- receiver thresholds, post-layout (klt pex)
*
* Post-layout counterpart of sim/se-receiver-dm-thresholds: identical circuit body, measurements and
* checks. The single .include below names the schematic-leg DUT shim (se_receiver_dm_pex_dut.spice:
* design/netlist/se_receiver_dm.spice with its .subckt declaration line reordered to the
* extracted header's pin order) -- the swap point klt pex re-points at the extracted
* netlist for the extracted-side leg. Every DUT instance line's nets are written in
* that same order, so one positional instance line serves both legs with the same
* net-to-pin mapping. The request supplies the .lib corner section, .temp and the
* supply sweep (vsup).
*
* Stimulus (unchanged from the committed bench): one DC sweep of the line input DM
* from 0 V to 3.0 V in 1 mV steps (3001 points), ideal source. 3.0 V is the lowest
* matrix supply, so the input never exceeds the receiver's own rail.


.include "se_receiver_dm_pex_dut.spice"

vsup vdd 0 dc 3.3
vi vdd vddr dc 0
vin in 0 dc 0
ehalf half 0 vol='v(vdd)/2'
xrx in rxdm vddr 0 se_receiver_dm

* ---- included: se_receiver_dm_pex_dut.spice ----
* se_receiver_dm_pex_dut.spice -- schematic-leg DUT for sim/se-receiver-dm-pex
*
* design/netlist/se_receiver_dm.spice with its .subckt declaration line's pin
* list reordered from the schematic symbol order (VDD VSS DM RXDM) to the order klt
* extract writes the extracted header in (DM RXDM VDD VSS, alphabetical; confirmed by a
* klt pex --extract-only probe of the committed GDS). klt pex reuses one positional
* instance line on both legs, so both sides must declare the same pin sequence, and
* the deck's instance lines carry their nets in the same order (same net-to-pin
* mapping on both legs). The reordered declaration is electrically identical (SPICE
* maps instance positions to the declared pin names) and every other byte is identical
* to the pinned netlist; the schematic leg must reproduce the committed record named in
* the pex run.py gate before any delta is read.
* se_receiver_dm -- exported by design/export_netlist.sh from design/se_receiver_dm.sch (xschem, sky130 symbols)
* Do not edit: edit the schematic and re-run the export.
** sch_path: design/se_receiver_dm.sch
.subckt se_receiver_dm DM RXDM VDD VSS
*.iopin VDD
*.iopin VSS
*.ipin DM
*.iopin RXDM
